WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.964
"Delicious." Hermes dabbed his mouth with a cloth and stood up from the dinner table. He glanced at Markos and Julia.

2
00:00:13.965 --> 00:00:20.212
"Too bad Markos and the girl forgot to get more eels, though. I would have liked a third helping."

3
00:00:20.213 --> 00:00:29.787
"I'm so sorry, Hermes," Markos' father, Nikolaos, said. "I thought we had plenty of eels. It won't happen again."

4
00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:37.017
"Come, my friend," Caerus told Hermes. "Let's find Dionysus and celebrate the fine evening."

5
00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:46.266
"Yes." Hermes shot Brody a frown. "Although I'm not much in the mood for celebrating after today's chariot practice."

6
00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:50.132
Without another word the two gods left.

7
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:56.342
Nikolaos frowned at his wife, who was helping Julia and the other girls clear the dishes.

8
00:00:56.343 --> 00:01:02.979
"That was an embarrassment," he said. "You know that eels are Hermes' favorite!"

9
00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:09.207
"How could I predict he'd eat twice as many as usual?" his wife retorted, sounding grumpy.

10
00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:17.831
She snapped her fingers at Markos. "Markos! Go to the agora right now and tell the vendor that we'll want more eels this week.

11
00:01:17.832 --> 00:01:22.218
We want only the freshest ones and plenty of them!"

12
00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:26.012
"Yes, Mother." Markos stood up.

13
00:01:26.013 --> 00:01:31.319
"We'll come along and help you, Markos," Julia said. "Right, Brody?"

14
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:37.669
"Huh?" Brody looked up from his meal. "I'm not finished eating."

15
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:45.668
"Come on," Julia said, yanking on his chiton so hard that Brody was afraid she was going to pull it right off.

16
00:01:45.669 --> 00:01:51.892
He glared at her. Back home he had barely noticed that Julia existed.

17
00:01:51.893 --> 00:01:57.411
She was just a nerd who never came to the football games or did anything else interesting.

18
00:01:57.412 --> 00:02:04.069
It was a lot harder to ignore her here in ancient Greece. When had she become so assertive?

19
00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:10.749
He sighed loudly and stood up. "Fine," he said.

20
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:17.090
"I'm exhausted after my long day of training for the Olympics, but whatever."

21
00:02:17.091 --> 00:02:22.593
He grabbed one last olive and tossed it into his mouth.

22
00:02:22.594 --> 00:02:27.496
Soon the three of them were walking toward the agora.

23
00:02:27.497 --> 00:02:31.358
"What do you think?" Julia asked Markos.

24
00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:37.886
"Is there any chance that Brody will get good enough at chariot racing in time to win at the Games?"

25
00:02:37.887 --> 00:02:41.181
"Why don't you ask me?" Brody said.

26
00:02:41.182 --> 00:02:47.970
"I'm the one who has to do it. And controlling a bunch of crazy wild horses isn't as easy as it looks."

27
00:02:47.971 --> 00:02:54.614
"It didn't look easy at all," Julia said. "That's exactly my point.

28
00:02:54.615 --> 00:02:57.598
What if you don't improve fast enough?

29
00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:02.844
If you don't impress Hermes, he might break his promise to let us leave."

30
00:03:02.845 --> 00:03:10.337
Brody shrugged. "I have more than a week to practice. Besides, who cares what Hermes thinks of me right now?

31
00:03:10.338 --> 00:03:16.423
If I look bad at chariot driving, he'll be even more impressed when I win on the big day!"

32
00:03:16.424 --> 00:03:23.591
Julia still looked worried. "I don't want to get stuck here in ancient Greece forever."

33
00:03:23.592 --> 00:03:30.138
She glanced over at Markos. "Sorry, Markos. I don't mean to offend you."

34
00:03:30.139 --> 00:03:35.254
"Don't worry, I'll win," Brody said. "End of story."

35
00:03:35.255 --> 00:03:37.959
By then they were entering the agora.

36
00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:42.207
Several young men were gathered near a fabric vendor's stall.

37
00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:48.866
Brody recognized most of them as other champions. A few waved to him.

38
00:03:48.867 --> 00:03:54.916
"Did you hear the news?" Apollo's champion called. "The mighty Alcides arrives soon."

39
00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:59.008
"We heard all about it," Brody replied.

40
00:03:59.009 --> 00:04:03.148
"So what? I'm glad we'll finally get the chance to see this guy."

41
00:04:03.149 --> 00:04:09.526
Artemis' champion shook his head. "I'm not so sure I want to see him," he said.

42
00:04:09.527 --> 00:04:14.893
"I overheard Artemis talking with Ares and Hestia, the goddess of the hearth and home.

43
00:04:14.894 --> 00:04:22.166
Zeus told them that Alcides strangled two enormous serpents with his bare hands when he was less than a year old!"

44
00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:32.729
"Serpents? That's nothing," said Demeter's champion. "I heard that Alcides killed a dozen men before he was ten years old!"

45
00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:41.808
"Well, I heard that Alcides eats human brains for breakfast," Artemis' champion added. "Zeus says it makes him smarter."

46
00:04:41.809 --> 00:04:45.505
"That makes sense," put in Ares' champion.

47
00:04:45.506 --> 00:04:52.388
"Because Ares told me that Alcides eats human muscles for lunch. It's supposed to make him stronger."

48
00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:57.862
Brody listened, not sure what to think about what the athletes were saying.

49
00:04:57.863 --> 00:05:01.789
All these rumors were getting pretty tiring though.

50
00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:08.437
Just then a sleek deer raced toward them, dodging around the people in the agora.

51
00:05:08.438 --> 00:05:12.543
"Whoa," Brody said. "Loose animal!"

52
00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:14.867
The deer stopped in front of the group.

53
00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:18.874
It seemed pretty tame, so Brody stepped toward it.

54
00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:24.304
He was about to grab the deer when it suddenly transformed into Artemis.

55
00:05:24.305 --> 00:05:31.731
"Whoa!" Brody said again. He couldn't get used to the way the gods could transform into animals!

56
00:05:31.732 --> 00:05:38.006
Artemis crooked her finger at her champion. "Come, my boy," she ordered.

57
00:05:38.007 --> 00:05:42.793
"You need to rest. We have much more training to do tomorrow."

58
00:05:42.794 --> 00:05:46.506
"Coming," her champion said.

59
00:05:46.507 --> 00:05:54.209
"I'd better go, too," one of the others said. "Ares will be looking for me."

60
00:05:54.210 --> 00:06:00.263
Before long Brody, Julia, and Markos were alone again.

61
00:06:00.264 --> 00:06:08.128
"Wow," Julia said. "This Alcides sounds really impressive. I'm surprised I've never heard of him.

62
00:06:08.129 --> 00:06:11.806
Though that story about the serpents seemed familiar. I think—"

63
00:06:11.807 --> 00:06:16.505
"You haven't heard of him?" Brody cut her off.

64
00:06:16.506 --> 00:06:21.342
"That's cool. It means Zeus is probably exaggerating, right?

65
00:06:21.343 --> 00:06:27.847
I mean, if Alcides was really that great, wouldn't we have studied him in social studies class?"

66
00:06:27.848 --> 00:06:37.933
"Maybe." Julia looked troubled. "Then again, it's not as if we could possibly learn everything about ancient Greece.

67
00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:46.430
Maybe Alcides really is a great hero, just not quite as great as the really famous ones like Heracles or Achilles."

68
00:06:46.431 --> 00:06:53.002
She sighed. "I wish I had my phone so I could look him up on the Internet."

69
00:06:53.003 --> 00:07:05.046
Markos looked uncomfortable. Brody had noticed that Markos looked that way whenever Brody and Julia discussed their lives in the future.

70
00:07:05.047 --> 00:07:11.660
"It's getting dark," Markos said. "We should tell the vendor about the eels and get home.

71
00:07:11.661 --> 00:07:24.718
Brody, you need to rest too. Tomorrow is likely to be a busy day."

